Cell[TextData[{
 "The new compiler function ",
 StyleBox["ContractAll", "Input",
  Background->RGBColor[1, 0.75, 0, 0.33]],
 " expands a contraction as a sum over all coordinates. The up-down index \
pairs are now coordinate symbols rather than summation indices. Each term in \
the following exhibit is a product of concrete components, not a further \
(recursive) contraction. We can tell not to contract when a coordinate symbol \
appears in pairs index positions."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.978193094907441*^9, 3.978193205848093*^9}, {
  3.9782151788712893`*^9, 3.9782151926911077`*^9}, {3.978215307594297*^9, 
